# PLAINTEXT PERSONAL-DATA DUMPS - never commit these.
# scripts/repair-personal-data-encoding.cjs and the app's own "Export backup"
# write DECRYPTED records here. This repo is the public track (see CLAUDE.md's
# personal-alpha/public-alpha split), so a stray `git add .` here would publish
# the owner's real medical records. Keep the directory local; delete the dumps
# once they've served their purpose.
backups/

# Editor/tool config snapshots. Five of these were committed to this repo by
# accident and sat in `git status` forever. They are a snapshot of a config
# that git history already records, so tracking them bought nothing and cost
# noise on every status - the exact hand-maintained-inventory rot CLAUDE.md
# warns about. If you want one back, `git log` has it.
.opencode/*.backup*
opencode.json.backup*
.opencode.json.backup*
